out.push(SAMPLE(['Ms Huda asked what four years have changed that is not about English, and Mrs Rizk said her Arabic refusals: she stopped writing the Arabic equivalent of we are unable in November and can date it, because the November letters and the October ones are both in the file, and of the eleven Arabic refusals she has written since, nine name the decision and two name an obstacle, and both obstacles are real. Ms Huda said that is not an English change at all, and Mrs Rizk said it is not, and it is the biggest thing the course has done to her, because the English units taught her to tell a decision from an incapacity and the distinction is not in English. Mrs Oueidat said hers is reading aloud: every certificate of accuracy, aloud, before signing, since June, which is about sixty, and she found three errors in the first fortnight and one of them was a date. Mr Attar said his is a question: he asks where a figure came from, out loud, in meetings, in Arabic, which he had never done at twenty-two and did first in January, four times since, and twice the answer was I do not know, and the two I do not knows have changed two decisions. Mrs Khoury said hers is about other people: she has stopped asking juniors to do things she cannot demonstrate, after eleven years of telling people to tighten it, and the evidence is one move taught and two instructions withdrawn. Dr Qabbani said he has nothing: four years, better English, and no practice outside it that has changed, and he has looked for a fortnight and is saying so because the room would otherwise hear nine answers and assume there were ten. Ms Huda said that is the most useful answer in the cycle, because a course that improves somebody\'s English has done what it said it would, and a room in which everybody reports a transformation has learnt to produce the answer a teacher wants. Mrs Tarabishi said hers is the plan, kept for everything over two thousand words since January, and the evidence is that her supervisor has asked the other three candidates for one, which is not her achievement. Mr Tayara said his is a filing cabinet, and nine of nine Saturday sheets filed since February against nineteen of fifty-two last year, and the change is not his either. And Mrs Khoury said the thing she will take away is Dr Qabbani\'s fortnight of looking.']));
