// ===================== 24.4 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('24.4  The one thing I would take out'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open, and ask for the replacement in the same breath. ⚠ **Six of ten had one and four produced a complaint, and the four wrote a replacement when they were asked to sit down and do it** — **in between two and eleven minutes, which is the whole measurable difference between a complaint and a criticism and should be timed in front of the room.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Criticisms with replacements: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **A cycle moved from position seven to position three; a cycle moved from C1 to B1.** **1, 3 and 5 name nothing that can be moved** — **_too much writing_, _I did not enjoy_, _too long_** — **and the room should be asked who could act on any of the three and how.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The thing has to be small enough to move, and this is where the cycle is won or lost.** **One cycle, four pages, a word, a box, three minutes of a stage, a unit\'s position** — **and _too much writing_ cannot be acted on by anybody, whatever its truth.** ⚠ **Then the finding, which is the room\'s and not the key\'s: all four usable replacements in this class moved something earlier and nobody asked for anything to be removed.** **Do not supply that: ask what the four have in common and let somebody see it** — **and if nobody does, leave it unsaid, because it is a finding about this class and not a law.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Ms Huda tells the room what happens to the criticisms and the key asks her to be exact, because the room has four years of reason to doubt it.** **They are written down verbatim, with the student\'s name and the cost, and sent to whoever wrote the course** — **and three criticisms from the B2 class of 2024 are in the books this room is holding: the seven-cycle unit, the figure in every house model, and the _I cannot yet_ box.** ⚠ **Say also, because it is true and it is the part that makes the rest credible, that the teacher is not the filter: the ones she thinks are wrong go up as well, and the figure in the house model is the one she argued against in 2024 and is the single thing students mention most.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** _Too much writing_ → ⚠ **a complaint: nothing to move.**   **2** _Move the mediation cycle from seven to three_ → **a criticism; the replacement is a position.**   **3** ⚠ _I did not enjoy the grammar_ → **a report of a feeling about a section.**   **4** _Put the mapping cycle at B1_ → **a criticism with a price: four pages at B1.**   **5** ⚠ _Some units are too long_ → **true of five of twenty-four and nameable, which is what makes it a complaint and not a fact.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
