out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Ms Huda asked for the one thing each of them would take out. Mrs Ajouz said the four years of silence about examinations, which she had asked about in 1.1 and been given no good answer to, and Unit 21 is the answer and it arrives three weeks before the end, and what it cost her is fourteen months, two test fees and ninety hours on one quarter of one paper; and her replacement is the mapping cycle at B1, where the deadline actually falls, not the whole unit but one cycle of four pages. Mr Attar said his is the board clinic, three minutes at the end of every report stage, eighty-four times in the book, which is four hours of a hundred and twenty, and his replacement is the same three minutes on the listener task of the next cycle, and he knows the answer to his own criticism and is saying it anyway because the question was what he would take out. Mrs Oueidat said hers is a word, mediate, which is the title of twelve cycles and is the wrong word for what they do, and her replacement is Review and Report, which is dull and accurate, and the cost of the word is three cycles she skipped in Book 1 because she thought they were about conflict resolution. Mrs Khoury said hers is the Language box at A2 and B1, eight paragraphs of reasons where a beginner needs six documents and a drill, with the reasons moved to B2. Ms Huda said she writes them down verbatim with the student\'s name and the cost, and they go to whoever wrote the course, and three criticisms from the B2 class of 2024 are in the book this room is holding. Mr Shihabi asked which three, and the seven-cycle unit instead of eight, the figure in every house model, and the I cannot yet box, which is now in all four levels. Mrs Tarabishi said that is a strange thing to be told at the end, and Mrs Khoury said it is what makes 24.6 a real document rather than an exercise. Mr Tayara asked about the criticisms that are wrong, and Ms Huda said they go up as well with no comment of hers, because she is not the filter and has been wrong about which ones were wrong. And Mrs Khoury said the thing she will take away is the shape of the four replacements in the room that are any good, because all four move something earlier and not one of them asks for anything to be removed, which is what four years of criticism from ten people who have paid for it in hours comes to: the whole of it is about order.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two findings and the second is the room\'s own.** **Three criticisms from a class of 2024 are in these books, which is what makes 24.6 a document rather than an exercise** — **and all four of the usable replacements in this class move something earlier, and nobody asked for anything to be removed.** **Ask what that means about four years of criticism from ten people who have paid for it in hours.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **A complaint offered as a criticism** → **four of ten, all repaired by writing.**   **2** **A thing too large to move** → **_the course should be shorter_.**   **3** ⚠ **A replacement that only adds** → **it has not been priced.**   **4** **A criticism withheld because the writer can answer it** → **say it anyway; Mr Attar\'s clinic.**   **5** ⚠ **_I may be wrong, but_** → **22.3\'s softening in front of a criticism.**   **6** **Heat** → **the thing criticised is four pages and has no feelings.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **The Language box, at A2 and B1 only** — **and she says plainly that she is not asking for it to be taken out of B2 or C1, where it is the best part of the page.** **The boundaries are what make the criticism actionable: a reader knows exactly how many pages are in question.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Miss Dandashi has the move after four days and cannot explain it; Ms Huda has taught it sixty times at A2 and has never explained it; her sixty learners do it.** **That is sixty against one** — **and it is the only evidence in the criticism that is not about the writer herself, which she says in the document.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Mrs Ajouz, who says the explanations are the reason she stayed** — **she arrived with a B2 from elsewhere and no method, and the reasons gave her a way of seeing what the drills were for.** **And the writer adds that if that case is the common one she is wrong and she cannot tell from inside one class of ten.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
