out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That nobody told her.** **It is true: nobody said it to her in four years** — **and the two sentences are on page forty-one of a key she has owned since 2022, so saying it blames a roomful of people for a page she did not turn.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the eleventh mediation of Book 2 and the last of the series, and it is the only one in which the document nobody has opened is a page of this course.** **Page forty-one of the A2 key says _do not teach the reason at A2; the reason arrives at B2, where there is something underneath it_** — **and it anticipates exactly what happened on the Friday, in a book Mrs Khoury has owned for four years and has never opened past the exercises.** ⚠ **Four things, in this order.** **First: nobody is at fault, for the last time — the leaver handed on the visible half, the arriver read thirteen words correctly, the teacher had no reason to quote an A2 key to a C1 student, and the key had said it since 2022.** **Second: Miss Dandashi corrected herself on the Saturday, before anybody told her anything, because a consequence is a better teacher than a reason** — **which is the sentence the whole course is built on and has never printed, and Ms Huda says it here, which is her third and last intervention.** **Third: the reason still waits two years, which is the hardest instruction in the unit and comes from the page, not from the teacher.** ⚠ **And fourth: Mrs Khoury repairs the consequence herself, in Arabic, in four sentences, to a man of forty-four** — **because the person who taught a move repairs what it did, and a teacher who lets a nineteen-year-old carry it has taught a second thing, which is that teaching is free.**'));
